    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 6 USER]\ne054\tJonah proposed restoring one moment of hesitation and adding a short scene earlier that shows the participant's obligations in the town.\ne055\tHe would keep the final sequence.\ne056\tI can imagine that working.\ne057\tBut he also wants the credit to read “A film by Jonah Vale and Mira Chen,” even though it is audio, because the showcase uses that language.\ne058\tI want “Reported by Mira Chen, sound and story by Jonah Vale.”\ne059\tHe hears my version as splitting the work into journalism and art.\n[Turn 6 ASSISTANT]\ne060\tHis edit proposal sounds like a substantive attempt to preserve uncertainty without dissolving the ending, though you should judge it in the cut rather than in description.\ne061\tThe credit disagreement is not merely wording; each version tells a story about what the work is.\ne062\tEqual top-line authorship plus a second line naming reporting, editing, and sound may acknowledge collaboration and labor, but only if neither of you experiences the top line as erasing the actual imbalance you are trying to name.",
